 "summary": "Gateway profile for the PowerLogic PM800: 126 Analog Inputs, 44 polled by default. Polled values cover phase, neutral and ground currents, voltages, real/reactive/apparent power per phase and total, true PF, frequency and real, reactive, apparent and conditional energy.",
 "bacnet_transport": [
  "BACnet IP"
 ],
 "firmware": null,
 "default_device_instance": null,
 "access_inferred": true,
 "notes": [
  "Built from Contemporary Controls' BASgatewayLX Modbus device profile Schneider_Electric__PM800_Meter_aLX.csv; the profile maps the registers in the maker's Modbus register document (https://www.ccontrols.com/support/dp/PM800.pdf).",
  "Object instances are the ones this profile assigns when it is loaded into the gateway. A site that edited or rebuilt the profile may use different instances.",
  "Only 44 of the 126 rows are flagged for polling in the profile; the rest are served only after you tick them in the gateway. Their descriptions say \"not polled by default\".",
  "The CSV has no read/write column: Analog/Binary Inputs are read-only and Analog/Binary Outputs are commandable (priority array), which is how the gateway maps them (access inferred). Descriptions give the Modbus register each object reads.",
  "Some names appear more than once in the profile as published (Energy Real Total (signed/absolute); Energy Reactive Total (signed/absolute); Energy Apparent...); they are kept as printed and told apart by instance."
 ],
